 ## Background
-Budget Plans were introduced in the `niivue` project to address the limitations of a single octree-focused chunk loading policy [S1, unofficial]. The design doc is located at `docs/budget-plans.md`, with remaining streaming work tracked in `docs/streaming-todos.md` [S1, unofficial]. The implementation includes fixes for chunk 0 eviction blanking the volume in WebGL2 and adapts to both WebGL2 and WebGPU backends [S1, unofficial]. The Exact Lattice Grid variant was added to support specific block counts in demos like the Zarr demo, which uses a "Blocks control" to choose factorizations closest to cubic [S1, unofficial].
+Originated in the Niivue project to address the limitation of having only one octree-focused policy, which was suitable for exploration but poor for whole-volume figures or frame-rate holding [S1, unofficial]. The design doc is located at `docs/budget-plans.md`, with remaining streaming work tracked in `docs/streaming-todos.md` [S1, unofficial].
 
